   "id": "reporting",
   "title": "Reporting",
   "icon": "▤",
   "sub": "Formats and the baseline",
   "kind": "pages",
   "pages": [
    {
     "id": "reporting",
     "title": "Reporting",
     "docTitle": "Reporting — format and worked example",
     "sub": "Templates and September baseline",
     "kind": "md",
     "file": "content/planning/reporting.md",
     "html": "<p>How results are reported to TenTrade, with a worked monthly report built from September 2026, the last month before the engagement. It doubles as the baseline.</p>\n<h3>Two reports</h3>\n<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Report</th><th>When</th><th>Length</th><th>For</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fortnightly update</td><td>Every second Friday</td><td>One page</td><td>Lyn and the Account Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly report</td><td>First working week of the month</td><td>Three to five pages</td><td>The brand, Lyn, the Account Manager</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Fortnightly update — template</h3>\n<ol><li><b>Sent in the last two weeks:</b> each campaign with audience, count, opens, clicks and deposits so far.</li><li><b>Journeys:</b> entries and exits per journey, anything paused or changed.</li><li><b>Changed:</b> fixes, new segments, new tags or rules.</li><li><b>Tests running:</b> what is being tested and the result so far.</li><li><b>Decisions needed:</b> anything waiting on the brand, with a date.</li></ol>\n<h3>Monthly report — template</h3>\n<ol><li><b>Summary:</b> three numbers (deposits from email, click rate, bounce rate) against last month and the baseline, and the three things we recommend next.</li><li><b>Journeys:</b> per journey, the people who entered, reached the goal and left, emails sent, click rate, deposits; changes made and why.</li><li><b>Campaigns:</b> per campaign, the same measures, with what worked and what did not.</li><li><b>List health:</b> mailable base, hard bounces, complaints, unsubscribes, inactive contacts suppressed.</li><li><b>Tests:</b> what was tested, the result, what we changed because of it.</li><li><b>Recommendations:</b> the monthly note (see the Strategy section).</li></ol>\n<h3>Worked example — September 2026 (baseline)</h3>\n<p>Built from Voyager’s reports on 3 October 2026. Deposits from email cannot be reported yet: the conversion rule has not been agreed and Voyager’s “Converted” figure has no known definition.</p>\n<h4>Summary</h4>\n<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>September 2026</th><th>Comment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Emails sent</td><td>224,046</td><td>Almost all from five webinar blasts</td></tr><tr><td>Delivered</td><td>98.8%</td><td>Healthy</td></tr><tr><td>Opened</td><td>7.0%</td><td>Low; inflated further by image pre-loading</td></tr><tr><td>Clicked</td><td>0.1%</td><td>Very low</td></tr><tr><td>Bounced</td><td>1.1%</td><td>Above the 0.5% we aim for</td></tr><tr><td>Complaints</td><td>3</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Failed before sending</td><td>6,143</td><td>Needs investigation (invalid addresses or provider rejections)</td></tr><tr><td>Deposits from email</td><td>not measurable</td><td>Conversion rule to be agreed</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Three things to do next:</b> segment every blast; add reminders and a follow-up by attendance to webinar invitations; agree the conversion rule.</p>\n<h4>Campaigns</h4>\n<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Campaign</th><th>Audience</th><th>Delivered</th><th>Open</th><th>Click</th><th>Read</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Webinar 1 Oct</td><td>24 managers’ clients, not traded in 90 days</td><td>147,890</td><td>6.5%</td><td>0.1%</td><td>The broadest send; dormant clients rarely open a webinar invitation cold</td></tr><tr><td>Webinar 18 Sep, send 1</td><td>Verified, never deposited</td><td>17,350</td><td>10.0%</td><td>0.2%</td><td>Best of the broad sends: a clearer audience</td></tr><tr><td>Webinar 18 Sep, send 2</td><td>Tag “18sept1”</td><td>19,174</td><td>7.3%</td><td>0.2%</td><td>Second send to an overlapping audience a day later</td></tr><tr><td>Webinar 18 Sep, send 3B</td><td>Verified, never deposited</td><td>17,002</td><td>8.3%</td><td>0.1%</td><td>Third send in four days; fatigue shows</td></tr><tr><td>Webinar 18 Sep, send 3A</td><td>Tag “18sept1”</td><td>19,165</td><td>5.5%</td><td>0.1%</td><td>Lowest open rate of the month</td></tr><tr><td>Partner blast 1</td><td>One partner’s clients, traded in the last 60 days</td><td>225</td><td>54%</td><td>4%</td><td>Active, relevant audience; partner relationship</td></tr><tr><td>Partner blast 2</td><td>Same partner, never deposited or traded</td><td>616</td><td>41%</td><td>1%</td><td>Still strong: the partner context matters</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Journeys</h4>\n<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Journey</th><th>Status</th><th>Comment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Verified but not deposited</td><td>Active, test tag only</td><td>16 delivered to test accounts; not yet live</td></tr><tr><td>Verified but not deposited — test 2</td><td>Active, test tag only</td><td>Loses half its contacts at the last branch</td></tr><tr><td>Panos Test</td><td>Active</td><td>Daily placeholder email to testers; switch off</td></tr><tr><td>Test</td><td>Draft</td><td>Never sent</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>List health</h4>\n<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Leads</td><td>111,709</td></tr><tr><td>Registered clients who never deposited</td><td>163,389</td></tr><tr><td>Clients with a first deposit over 30 days ago (sendable)</td><td>43,209</td></tr><tr><td>Hard-bounce suppression in place</td><td>Not confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Re-permission rule for inactive contacts</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Tests</h4>\n<p>None ran in September. From October, one test at a time: first the subject line of the welcome webinar invitation (A/B, 50/50, winner by click rate after 1,000 sends per version).</p>"
    }
   ]
